            name: 'Policy gradients and PPO',
            definition: 'Policy-gradient methods train a policy network directly by making actions that led to better-than-expected returns more likely; PPO adds a clipped objective that keeps each update small and safe.',
            problem: 'Value-based methods like Q-learning struggle with huge or continuous action spaces — and a language model\'s "action" is a choice among tens of thousands of tokens. Policy gradients optimise the policy itself and handle such spaces naturally. PPO made them stable enough to use widely, including in classic RLHF for chat models.',
